RenderingDevice: frame queue and pipeline cache without a window

A RenderingDevice created without a main window runs a single frame in
flight and skips the pipeline cache, so an embedder rendering offscreen
gets no CPU/GPU overlap and recompiles pipelines at every launch.

set_surfaceless_frame_queue(true) and set_surfaceless_pipeline_cache(true),
called before initialize(), give the windowless singleton the project's
frame queue and the pipeline cache.

frame_signal_semaphore_add() adds a semaphore to the current frame's last
submission, so the embedder can export the frame's completion (a sync_file)
instead of waiting for it.

Applied by godot/CMakeLists.txt on top of GODOT_GIT_REF.

